# Scacelith - Türkçe
# Translation of assets/i18n/en.lang (same keys, same {n}). Plurals: one|other; a noun after a number
# stays singular in Turkish ("1 hamle", "5 hamle"), so both forms are usually the same words.
# Register: formal "siz" in sentences, instructions and questions, as in Microsoft and Apple Turkish
# software; buttons, menu entries and control descriptions are bare imperatives or noun phrases in
# sentence case ("Kaydet", "Yeni oyun"). Titles in capitals with Turkish casing (i -> İ, ı -> I).
# Terms follow glossary/tr.md: game = oyun (never parti/maç), coach = eğitmen, resign = terk etmek,
# rated / casual = puanlı / puansız, time control = süre kontrolü, scoresheet = notasyon kâğıdı,
# illegal move = kural dışı hamle, legal move = geçerli hamle, flag fall = süre doldu.
# No suffix is ever attached to a placeholder ({0} may be a name, a number or a word): the ending goes
# on a noun next to it ("{0} sunucusuna", "{0} adlı oyuncunun"), a separate word (ile, için, olarak,
# sonra, tarafından) follows it, or it stands after a colon.

